League Night is a league tracker for darts and other pub and club games —
players or teams, a season schedule, standings, live scoring and knock-out
tournaments, shared with everyone in the league. It was conceived, designed
and written by Charles Adams as an independent personal project:

  * Built on personally owned hardware, using a personal Anthropic (Claude)
    subscription paid for by the author.
  * Developed in the author's personal GitHub account (eagleadams86).
  * No employer equipment, funding, source code or libraries were used.
  * No employer confidential or proprietary information is present in this
    repository or in the application. Its only data is what league members
    enter for their own league — names, fixtures and scores — kept in their
    own browsers and, when they choose to sign in, in a Firebase project the
    author pays for. The demo league is invented.

